  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Hurry Up & Wait** (1 other source): Sam Kininger plays alto saxophone on this one [2]\n- **It's Your Thing** (1 other source): Sam Kininger also plays alto saxophone on this track [2]\n- **Lenny** (1 other source): Lenny flows directly into Turn It Out without a break [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Teen Town**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Cissy Strut**: back after 72 archived shows (481 days); rare: 6 archived performances [3]\n- **The Chicken**: back after 72 archived shows (481 days); rare: 6 archived performances [3]\n- **Spider**: mythic rare: 2 archived performances [3]\n- **Headin' Home**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2001-06-19.cmc621.sbd.matrix.flac16** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 15 songs; 191 min [1]\n- **soulive2001-06-19.shnf**: matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 9 songs; 96 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: Al [1]\n- Free early-evening show at Copley Square, part of the Boston Globe's jazz and blues festival [1]\n- Sam Kininger sat in on alto saxophone [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2001-06-19.cmc621.sbd.matrix.flac16**: taped by Pete Costello and Eric McRoberts; transferred by Eric McRoberts; source: On Stage Audience/SBD Matrix [1]. Also: Pete Costello recorded from on stage with Schoeps mics plus a soundboard feed, mixed and digitized at 44.1kHz; Eric McRoberts transferred and fixed it in 2014 [1]\n- **soulive2001-06-19.shnf**: taped by Pete Costello; transferred by Steve Gatzos; source: Matrix: (On Stage) Schoeps cmc621->Lunatec 316+SBD->Behringer MX-802A->AD2K+ @44.1kHz [2]",
